<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Coorg</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1834 CE (approx.) · capital Madikeri</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A hill kingdom of the Western Ghats ruled by the Haleri Rajas until the British annexed it in 1834.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1600 a member of the Haleri family, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lingayatism">Lingayat</a> house related to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keladi-nayakas">Nayakas of Ikkeri</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keladi">Keladi</a>), established himself in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kodagu">Kodagu</a>, the hilly country at the source of the Kaveri. His successors built a kingdom with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madikeri">Madikeri</a> (Mercara).</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Rajas ruled the warrior <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kodava-people">Kodava</a> landholders through their own officials. Coorg resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan of Mysore</a>, who occupied it at intervals from the 1770s. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dodda-vira-rajendra">Dodda Vira Rajendra</a> regained the throne and allied with the British in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-mysore-wars">Anglo-Mysore wars</a>. The economy rested on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> and forest produce; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> arrived later.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chikka-vira-rajendra">Chikka Vira Rajendra</a> quarrelled with the Company, a British force deposed him in 1834 and annexed Coorg. It became a province of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/british-raj">British India</a>, then a state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> until 1956, when it joined <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mysore-state">Mysore State</a>, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-coorg.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Coorg" width="320" height="454"><figcaption>Image: by PlaneMad; derivative work by Nayvik · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kodagu_in_Karnataka_(India).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1834 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Madikeri</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Dodda Vira Rajendra, Chikka Vira Rajendra</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kodava, Kannada</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kodagu Kingdom, Coorg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1717&amp;focus=kingdom-of-coorg" aria-label="Kingdom of Coorg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6760 1715 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Coorg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7080 1971L7107 1971M7080 1971L7364 1601"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7107 1971h0M7364 1601h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7080 1971h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7080 1971h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Madikeri. <a href="/atlas?year=1717&amp;focus=kingdom-of-coorg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

